{
  "$comment": "Everything the wall game plays by (distances in world units, the wall's cells `cell` across; times in seconds). wall: its size (a portrait block, the same on every screen), `breakShare`: the share of its cells that brings it down (its HP is that share, so the bar and the hole are the same thing), `noise`: how much the weak lines steer a hit, `gap`: how far behind the next gate is (even, and farther than the camera's off the wall, so it's walked through). camera: upright, the wall's between the bar at the top and the cards, `clear` off both (the HUD's units), taking at most `tall` of the screen's height; on a wide screen (from its `aspect` on) the share it takes and how far up it stands (`floorAt`); `side`: the frame seen each side of it on a narrow one. wallHp: by number (past the list: the last x `hpGrowth`^n). wallMaterials: wall by wall; round again (from `roundFrom`) after the last, in other colours. materials: `look` (the pattern), colours, `core`: the colour of its deepest layers, `dust`, `chip`: debris size, `hit`: its sound, `cash`: what its damage pays (1 if not given), `room`: the colour of the dark behind it (and a touch of the grey round it), `accent`: of the lights on its gate. punch: the damage, and PUNCH HARDER: the first level's given (after wall 1), and later ones at the walls in `given` (a tool each) to players who haven't bought up to that level by then, each next costs `cost` x `costGrowth`^n, `mult` its effect level by level (the last repeats). bricks: what a wall brings (base + perWall x its number). crew: helpers (the first of the first kind's given when its wall's reached); each copy costs x `crewGrowth` more; there from wall `wall` on (ever reached); `dps`: damage a second each; `every`: seconds between one's hits; `size`: how big; `z`: how far from the wall it stands; `style`: leap (headbutts) or throw; `shows`: how many are drawn. crewBoosts: the crew's own boosts: from `at` copies on, x `mult`, for `bricks` (+ `typeBricks` for each place down the list). boosts: the others, there from a wall or a number of copies on. weak: the weak spot (from wall `wall`): `mult` its hit, `radius` around it that counts (of the screen's height), hit again within `window` the combo goes up a step (`combo`, `comboSteps` of them to start with). shows: from which wall (ever reached) on the boosts' row and the wardrobe's button are there. medal: the one behind the wall, from wall `wall` on; a wall down brings its number of them. enemies: what waits behind some walls (`on`: false, and there's nothing: the game as it was without them; ?enemies=0 or 1 tries it, and so does the debug panel). boss: behind every `every`th wall, which is of `material`; `hp`: a share of the wall's, `seconds` to beat it in; beaten, `cash` (x the wall's HP), `bricks` and `medals` more; kinds in turn (with each rewind, from the next), each boss bigger than the one before (`grow`, and `growRun` for each rewind, at most `most`) and, every `colorEvery` bosses and with each rewind, in the next of `colors`: `paint` bone only the bones, `hue` all of it turned to that hue (from its own, `base`; at least this vivid, `sat`). `pair`: two of them, half the health each (`x` along the gate, `next` colours on). minions: behind every `every`th wall, from wall `from` (not a boss's); `count` of them (one more every `more` walls, at most `most`), `hp` each (a share of the wall's), `cash` for one (x its HP); kinds in turn. farm: the minions that come while a boss that got away isn't called back. rewind: from wall `wall` (reached): back to wall 1 without cash, bricks or crew, PUNCH HARDER and boosts kept, all damage + `perMedal` for each medal, for good. tools: a new one with every PUNCH HARDER level from `from` on: the types in turn, in the next colour (tiers, for the metal; `glow`: it shines) every `perTier` levels; `bite`: how a hit spreads (wide: across the face, deep: into it).",
